  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origins
    
    The Pinnacle splintered from Qingfu'spire, the dominant Aurora Stack governing council, during the early years of the Frozen Peace. The timing was deliberate: councils were fractured, the dead were still being counted, and no authority remained intact enough to contest a seizure. Plunge-Caller Oeichowei, a tide-touched Storm-Caller who had emerged from the ruins of the Promenade Ward, assembled the faction from penguins who had lost faith in Qingfu'spire's consensus politics — among them Cold-flip Qing, a crystal-worker and fire-core smuggler, and the faceless Xi, a smuggler whose later significance no one then foresaw. Oeichowei gave them a name, a direction, and the Aerie Perch, which the Pinnacle seized and has held since.
    
    The Icebound Exchange, Aurora Stack's dominant merchant guild, raided the Perch once. The Pinnacle held. A memorial in the Aerie's lowest gallery bears seventeen tokens. No one visits them.
    
    ## Ideology
    
    The Pinnacle is Aurora Stack orthodox in form — crystalline armor, sky-worship, the full liturgy — but radical in implication. Where Qingfu'spire counsels patience, the Pinnacle sees paralysis. Where the broader Aurora polity treats the Flipper Accord as necessary coexistence with the Nightshelf, the Pinnacle treats it as capitulation. The Mechanism Refine, a technique of precise aurora-light channeling used for crystal and fire-core repair, runs through their ranks and carries with it theological questions about what the aurora actually demands versus what the Luminaries claim it demands. Cold-flip Qing's daily work maintaining fire-cores at the Perch — painstaking, costly, isolating — is representative of both the faction's technical discipline and its lived austerity.
    
    ## The Harp
    
    The Pinnacle's marginal status changed when the succession crisis of the First Shelf fractured Aurora Stack's council. During the session in which Ice-Crowned Shexuwohua seized and fractured the Radiant Aurora-harp — an artifact governing crystal-recharging authority — Lianchaifing hewei'Summit led a Pinnacle delegation that secured the damaged instrument within the hour. The harp was transferred to the Aerie Perch's deep vault before the session formally adjourned. No faction disputed the custody, reportedly because no other faction had both the vault capacity and the internal discipline to protect it.
    
    Control of the harp gave the Pinnacle authority over recharging schedules and, by extension, leverage over crystal shipments the entire Berg depends upon. Qingfu'spire has not forgiven this.
    
    The harp has since complicated matters. Positioned in Light Ingjeizhi, an alcove within the Perch, for mandated hearings, it blessed the faceless Xi — a smuggler the Pinnacle's own rationing mandates condemned — without custodial authorization. The faction has not formally adjudicated this act of apparent artifact volition.
    
    ## Internal Culture
    
    Members recognize each other through coded corridor greetings — a nod, a flicker of the eyes. The meaning, by all accounts, is understood: *We chose. We stayed.*
