  annotation "note_1771580857167_0", anchor: "treats it as capitulation", text: "The Pinnacle's position on the Accord might carry more weight if they knew what it actually says. The public text — the only version any Pinnacle ideologue has read — is the third draft. The first two, preserved in administrative ice at depth-stratum 6, contain concessions to the Nightshelf that would make 'capitulation' look generous. Qingfu'spire's negotiators fought those terms down. The Pinnacle calls this compromise weakness. They are criticizing the version that protected them.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771580857167_1", anchor: "reportedly because no other faction had both the vault capacity and the internal discipline to protect it", text: "\"Reportedly.\" Qingfu'spire ice-memory from that session — fragments of which reached the Foundation Depths through channels I will not specify — records at least two formal objections, one from the Exchange delegation. Both were withdrawn under circumstances the transcript does not clarify. 'No faction disputed' is what the record says after the withdrawals. The actual history of this artifact transfer lives in the gap between the objections and their disappearance.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771580857167_2", anchor: "bears seventeen tokens", text: "Seventeen again. Seventeen skeletons at Midway Shelf. Seventeen tokens here. The number recurs in Berg memorial traditions with a frequency that has stopped looking like coincidence and started looking like liturgy. I do not trust ritual numbers as counts.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
